  "note": "An ARC_WAYPOINT leg from (0, 0, -10) to (0, 2e-7, -20) with arc angle 2.48 rad: a climb of 10 m (so the leg is not zero length, SCurve.cpp:80) with a horizontal chord of 2e-7 m. SCurve::calculate_track (SCurve.cpp:88) takes the arc branch because the chord length 2e-7 is_positive (>= FLT_EPSILON, 1.19e-7), and its comment says the radius is then positive; the radius chord / (2 |sin(1.24)|) = 1.06e-7 is below FLT_EPSILON, so project_scurve_onto_track (SCurve.cpp:678) finds !is_positive(arc.radius_ne), raises invalid_arg_or_result and clears the leg. The two guards disagree. A mission item cannot produce this chord (Location resolution 1e-7 deg, about 1.1 cm); the assumption now excludes arc legs (arc_rad = 0). Inputs added later (12: the `_seq` call-order fields and signals) are 0/false: fixed order, the steps are unchanged.",
